{
 "schema": "ultimate-radar/m3-team-labels@1",
 "possession": "p0001",
 "labelled_by": "claude-opus-5, 2026-09-13",
 "frames_source": "the same 20 held-out frames as eval/m2/labels.json (seed 20260827)",
 "what_was_judged": [
  "Every in-bounds box in those 20 frames, rendered by tools.m3_label render:",
  "the whole figure with the detection box drawn on it and the surroundings",
  "visible, so the label is attached to the person the box bounds rather than",
  "to whoever happens to be in the crop.",
  "",
  "sol    = light kit (Austin Sol): white jersey, blue or pink shorts",
  "chill  = dark kit (Minnesota Wind Chill): black jersey and shorts",
  "ref    = on-field official, black and white vertically striped shirt",
  "crew   = camera operator or photographer, almost always at the far boards",
  "unsure = the box bounds a Sol player and a Chill player together, so there",
  "         is no correct team for it",
  "",
  "35 close calls were settled by re-rendering them at 6-8x with more context",
  "(tools.m3_label zoom); eval/m3/zoom_a.png .. zoom_d.png are those renders.",
  "f37 #8 was corrected from chill to sol that way, and f210 #6 from a misread",
  "'28' to '23' - two players on one team cannot wear the same number, which is",
  "what prompted the second look.",
  "",
  "Corrected on a second look at 7x (zoom_e.png): f95 #12 is a Sol player with a",
  "Chill player clipped at the box edge, not the other way round; f47 #4 spans a",
  "Chill and a Sol player equally and became unsure."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "These are the agent's own labels, not an independent human's - the same",
  "caveat as eval/m2/labels.json, and it binds harder here: a 99 % gate on",
  "~235 items means two mistakes spends the whole budget.",
  "",
  "Two boxes (f327 #1 and #5) bound a thrower and the defender marking them in",
  "one box. They are labelled unsure and excluded from the team gate, because",
  "no team assignment for them can be right. They are counted and reported",
  "rather than quietly dropped. M2 recorded the same pair as its only class of",
  "miss.",
  "",
  "**These labels disagree with eval/m2/labels.json on three frames, and the",
  "disagreement is not resolved in M2's favour.** M2 counted people per frame;",
  "this pass judged every box individually at 2-8x with the box outline drawn",
  "on it. On f194, f210 and f226 M2 counted one, two and one more non-player",
  "respectively than this pass finds. Every f210 box was then re-examined at 7x",
  "(zoom_d.png): all fourteen are players, four of them Chill players wearing",
  "numbers 28, 23, 51 and 4. The far-side figures M2 may have read as crew sit",
  "at soccer y = 11.6 to 16.0, several yards inside the far sideline at +20.58,",
  "at height ratios 0.64 to 0.88. M2's own caveat allows about +/-1 per crowded",
  "frame; this is that, plus one frame at +/-2.",
  "",
  "The consequence is that M2's measured false-positive rate of 1.35/frame was",
  "slightly pessimistic. The honest reading of both passes together is that the",
  "true in-bounds non-player count over these 20 frames is 23, not 27. M3's",
  "reject gate is measured against 23 and says so."
 ],
